---
---

<dialog class="mc mc--lab" data-lab-dialog="posters" aria-labelledby="lab-posters-title">
  <div class="mc__bar">
    <h2 id="lab-posters-title" class="mc__title">Poster wall</h2>
    <button type="button" class="mc__close" data-mc-close aria-label="Close the poster wall">✕</button>
  </div>

  <!-- Horizontal Tab Strip -->
  <ol class="clean lab-tabs" aria-label="Research posters, newest first">
    <li>
      <button type="button" class="lab-tab" data-poster-for="p-aeroscan" aria-pressed="true">
        <span class="lab-tab__year">2026</span>
        <span class="lab-tab__title">AeroScan Tactical Edge AI</span>
      </button>
    </li>
    <li>
      <button type="button" class="lab-tab" data-poster-for="p-spam-classifier" aria-pressed="false">
        <span class="lab-tab__year">2025</span>
        <span class="lab-tab__title">Indonesian Spam & Slang NLP</span>
      </button>
    </li>
    <li>
      <button type="button" class="lab-tab" data-poster-for="p-omr-grader" aria-pressed="false">
        <span class="lab-tab__year">2025</span>
        <span class="lab-tab__title">Automated OMR Sheet Grader</span>
      </button>
    </li>
    <li>
      <button type="button" class="lab-tab" data-poster-for="p-trash-classification" aria-pressed="false">
        <span class="lab-tab__year">2024</span>
        <span class="lab-tab__title">Waste Sorting InceptionV3</span>
      </button>
    </li>
  </ol>

  <div class="mc__body">
    <!-- Poster 1: AeroScan -->
    <article class="poster" id="p-aeroscan" data-poster-panel="p-aeroscan" aria-label="Poster: AeroScan: Tactical Edge AI & Aerial Surveillance">
      <header class="poster__head">
        <div class="poster__id">
          <h3 class="poster__title">AeroScan: Tactical Edge AI & Aerial Surveillance</h3>
          <p class="poster__sub">Autonomous Edge Intelligence Lab · 2025 – Present</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="poster__cols">
        <div>
          <h4 class="brief__label">Abstract</h4>
          <p>
            Can learned evaluators and FP16-quantized YOLOv11x models perform ultra-low-latency military aircraft detection and tracking across multi-camera 4K feeds directly on NVIDIA Jetson hardware?
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="brief__label">Findings</h4>
          <ul class="poster__list">
            <li>YOLOv11x achieved 99.4% mAP50 and 87.2% mAP50-95 on aerial reconnaissance benchmarks across 5 military aircraft classes (B-2, F-16, F-22, F-35, Su-57).</li>
            <li>TensorRT 10 FP16 engine compilation cut end-to-end inference latency down to 3.2 ms/frame (>310 FPS throughput) on embedded edge accelerators.</li>
            <li>Edge tracking pipeline processes asynchronous RTSP video feeds via GStreamer hardware NVDEC with zero host CPU memory bottleneck.</li>
            <li>Multi-threaded FastAPI backend broadcasts real-time GeoJSON radar coordinates and confidence metrics over WebSocket at sub-10ms intervals.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h4 class="brief__label">Implications</h4>
        <p>
          Enables localized tactical aerial tracking and radar synchronization without cloud dependency, remaining fully operational in electronic-warfare RF-denied environments.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h4 class="brief__label">How it runs</h4>
        <figure class="flow" aria-label="How AeroScan Tactical Edge AI runs, step by step">
          <figcaption class="flow__bar">
            <span class="flow__name">AEROSCAN_PIPELINE.EXE</span>
            <span class="flow__lights" aria-hidden="true">
              <i></i><i></i><i></i>
            </span>
          </figcaption>
          <ol class="flow__stages">
            <li class="flow__step">
              <div class="flow__stage">
                <span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">01</span>
                <div class="flow__text">
                  <p class="flow__label">Video Ingestion</p>
                  <p class="flow__detail">Multi-camera 4K RTSP stream demuxing and hardware decoding via GStreamer NVDEC.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <span class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">▼</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flow__step">
              <div class="flow__stage">
                <span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">02</span>
                <div class="flow__text">
                  <p class="flow__label">TensorRT Quantization</p>
                  <p class="flow__detail">FP16 engine optimization with layer-fusion cutting inference down to 3.2ms.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <span class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">▼</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flow__step">
              <div class="flow__stage">
                <span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">03</span>
                <div class="flow__text">
                  <p class="flow__label">Ensemble Detection</p>
                  <p class="flow__detail">Multi-scale YOLOv11x inference classifying military aircraft airframes with 99.4% mAP.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <span class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">▼</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flow__step">
              <div class="flow__stage">
                <span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">04</span>
                <div class="flow__text">
                  <p class="flow__label">Radar Coordinate Mapping</p>
                  <p class="flow__detail">Camera homography and elevation projection mapping 2D bounding boxes to 3D radar coordinates.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
              <p class="flow__loop">
                <span aria-hidden="true">↺ </span>Confidence &lt; 0.85 → Temporal multi-frame consensus buffer
              </p>
              <span class="flow__arrow" aria-hidden="true">▼</span>
            </li>
            <li class="flow__step">
              <div class="flow__stage">
                <span class="flow__num" aria-hidden="true">05</span>
                <div class="flow__text">
                  <p class="flow__label">WebSocket Telemetry</p>
                  <p class="flow__detail">Sub-10ms binary GeoJSON broadcast streaming target trajectories to tactical ground display.</p>
                </div>
              </div>
            </li>
          </ol>
        </figure>
      </div>

      <h4 class="brief__label">Methods</h4>
      <ul class="stack-chips">
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #EE4C2C">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">PyTorch</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #00FFFF">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">YOLOv11</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #76B900">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">TensorRT FP16</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #76B900">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">NVIDIA Jetson</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #009688">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">FastAPI</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #5C3EE8">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">OpenCV</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #3776AB">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Python</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #2496ED">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Docker</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="poster__links">
        <a class="mc-btn" href="/dev#aeroscan">Full debrief →</a>
        <a class="mc-btn" href="https://github.com/Zulfan15" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Code ↗</a>
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- Poster 2: Spam & Slang Normalizer -->
    <article class="poster" id="p-spam-classifier" data-poster-panel="p-spam-classifier" hidden aria-label="Poster: SMS & WhatsApp Spam Detection with Indonesian Slang Normalization">
      <header class="poster__head">
        <div class="poster__id">
          <h3 class="poster__title">SMS & WhatsApp Spam Detection with Indonesian Slang Normalization</h3>
          <p class="poster__sub">ITENAS Undergraduate Thesis · Bandung, ID · Feb 2025 – Jan 2026</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="poster__cols">
        <div>
          <h4 class="brief__label">Abstract</h4>
          <p>
            How do Indonesian colloquial slang, character obfuscation (leetspeak), and morphological abbreviations impact spam detection accuracy, and can a lexical normalizer restore classification precision above 99.5%?
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="brief__label">Findings</h4>
          <ul class="poster__list">
            <li>Baseline Multinomial Naive Bayes suffered an 18.4% performance drop when exposed to adversarial Indonesian slang and SMS obfuscations.</li>
            <li>Engineered a dictionary-assisted slang normalizer mapping 1,500+ Indonesian colloquial terms, typo variations, and alphanumeric leetspeak into standard Bahasa Indonesia.</li>
            <li>Achieved 99.56% classification accuracy, 99.42% precision, and 99.70% recall across a verified corpus of 4,000+ SMS and WhatsApp fraud messages.</li>
            <li>Built an asynchronous FastAPI inference service and Streamlit interactive dashboard with real-time text obfuscation highlighting.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h4 class="brief__label">Implications</h4>
        <p>
          Demonstrates that targeted lexical preprocessing outperforms parameter-heavy large language models for localized Indonesian telecom spam filtering while running at 2.4ms latency per text.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h4 class="brief__label">Methods</h4>
      <ul class="stack-chips">
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #F7931E">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Multinomial Naive Bayes</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #F7931E">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">TF-IDF N-Grams</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #3776AB">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Slang Lexical Expansion</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #F7931E">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Scikit-Learn</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #009688">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">FastAPI</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #FF4B4B">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Streamlit</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #150458">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Pandas</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="poster__links">
        <a class="mc-btn" href="/dev#thesis-defense">Full debrief →</a>
        <a class="mc-btn" href="https://github.com/Zulfan15" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Code ↗</a>
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- Poster 3: OMR Grader -->
    <article class="poster" id="p-omr-grader" data-poster-panel="p-omr-grader" hidden aria-label="Poster: Automated OMR Answer Sheet Grader">
      <header class="poster__head">
        <div class="poster__id">
          <h3 class="poster__title">Automated OMR Answer Sheet Grader</h3>
          <p class="poster__sub">Applied Computer Vision Lab · Sep 2025 – Nov 2025</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="poster__cols">
        <div>
          <h4 class="brief__label">Abstract</h4>
          <p>
            Can computer vision replace expensive dedicated optical mark reading scanners by using adaptive homography perspective transforms and morphological bubble contour detection on ordinary smartphone photos?
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="brief__label">Findings</h4>
          <ul class="poster__list">
            <li>4-point adaptive perspective transform accurately corrects rotational tilt, keystoning, and paper warping from handheld smartphone camera captures.</li>
            <li>Morphological contour detection clusters answer bubble grids with 99.8% precision across 100+ simulated exam answer sheets.</li>
            <li>Threshold-based pixel density measurement reliably distinguishes between marked, unmarked, and incompletely erased pencil bubbles.</li>
            <li>Generates instant scoring reports, detailed per-question analytics, and automated CSV export for academic grading portals.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h4 class="brief__label">Implications</h4>
        <p>
          Provides an affordable, decentralized grading solution for schools and universities without dedicated hardware scanners.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h4 class="brief__label">Methods</h4>
      <ul class="stack-chips">
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #5C3EE8">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">OpenCV</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #5C3EE8">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Homography Transform</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #5C3EE8">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Bubble Contour Masking</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #013243">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">NumPy</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #3776AB">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Python</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="poster__links">
        <a class="mc-btn" href="/dev#omr-grader">Full debrief →</a>
        <a class="mc-btn" href="https://github.com/Zulfan15" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Code ↗</a>
      </p>
    </article>

    <!-- Poster 4: Trash Classification -->
    <article class="poster" id="p-trash-classification" data-poster-panel="p-trash-classification" hidden aria-label="Poster: Trash Classification with InceptionV3">
      <header class="poster__head">
        <div class="poster__id">
          <h3 class="poster__title">Trash Classification with InceptionV3</h3>
          <p class="poster__sub">Deep Learning & Computer Vision · Mar 2024 – Jul 2024</p>
        </div>
      </header>

      <div class="poster__cols">
        <div>
          <h4 class="brief__label">Abstract</h4>
          <p>
            How effectively does deep transfer learning with InceptionV3 bottleneck feature extraction generalize to automated recyclable waste sorting under variable lighting and complex backgrounds?
          </p>
        </div>
        <div>
          <h4 class="brief__label">Findings</h4>
          <ul class="poster__list">
            <li>Evaluated across 6 waste categories: cardboard, glass, metal, paper, plastic, and general trash.</li>
            <li>InceptionV3 pre-trained on ImageNet achieved 94.6% classification accuracy after fine-tuning top inception blocks with spatial dropout (0.4) and Adam optimizer.</li>
            <li>Real-time data augmentation (affine rotations, shear, zooming, brightness jittering) reduced overfitting on underrepresented plastic classes.</li>
            <li>Deployed into an interactive testing interface for real-time webcam waste recognition.</li>
          </ul>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h4 class="brief__label">Implications</h4>
        <p>
          Demonstrates viability of low-cost smart sorting bins capable of automated multi-material recycling segregation at source.
        </p>
      </div>

      <h4 class="brief__label">Methods</h4>
      <ul class="stack-chips">
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #FF6F00">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">TensorFlow</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #D00000">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Keras</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #FF6F00">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">InceptionV3</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #FF6F00">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Transfer Learning</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #3776AB">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">Python</span>
        </li>
        <li class="stack-chip" style="--brand: #013243">
          <span class="stack-chip__name">NumPy</span>
        </li>
      </ul>

      <p class="poster__links">
        <a class="mc-btn" href="/dev#inception-v3">Full debrief →</a>
        <a class="mc-btn" href="https://github.com/Zulfan15" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Code ↗</a>
      </p>
    </article>
  </div>
</dialog>
